// The middle of `c ? x : y`. With nothing there, `c ?: y` (a GNU form), the value
// is c when c is not zero: the middle is c's own node, which says so to the
// lowering (tern_elvis), where c is computed once.
cond_mid(int[] pos, int left) {
  int a = left;
  if(at_text(pos, ":") == 0) {
    a = parse_expr(pos);
  }
} return int a;
given boot_a given lexfix stdin ": y" ([0], 5):(5)
given boot_a given lexfix stdin "2 : y" ([0], 5):(0)
